  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Mubritinib may interact with CD276 antigen through a series of molecular targets. Specifically, Mubritinib is predicted to target DNA polymerase iota, which is in turn targeted by multiple compounds, including 2-((4-(Ethylamino)-6-methoxy-1,3,5-triazin-2-yl)amino)-2-methylpropiononitrile, (6S,10S)-6,10,14-trimethylpentadecan-2-one, and Guangsangon K. All of these compounds are linked to the CD276 antigen, indicating a potential pathway where Mubritinib could exert its effect by targeting DNA polymerase iota, which is a common target of these molecules. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust relationship, though the exact mechanism of Mubritinib's interaction with CD276 remains unclear. The evidence supports a possible role of DNA polymerase iota in mediating the effect of Mubritinib on CD276, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm this relationship.",
